      "message": "The default setting for CONFIG_SYS_CLOCK_TICKS_PER_SEC on the native posix target is 100, so the tick is 10ms.\n\nThis change causes tests that wait on a deferred action by sleeping 10ms or less to fail.\n\nFor example - changing the sleep [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/test/amd/src/amd_power.c;l\u003d544) from 10 to 11 ms allows the test to pass with this change.\n\nI see some other tests set the tick rate to [10 KHz](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3398505).  You can fix the other tests by making a similar change.\n\nHowever, this change adds extra latency for processing interrupts - 100 us for Nuvoton and about 30 us for ITE.\n\nHow about leaving the K_NO_WAIT, but explicitly reschedule if -EBUSY is returned?\n\n```\n\t\trv \u003d k_work_reschedule(work, delay);\n\n\t\tif (rv \u003d\u003d -EBUSY \u0026\u0026 K_TIMEOUT_EQ(delay, K_NO_WAIT)) {\n\t\t\tdelay \u003d K_TICKS(1);\n\t\t\trv \u003d k_work_reschedule(work, delay);\n\t\t}\n\n```",
